1: # P3K.65. The two actual OS49 fan returns
2: 
3: Audit draft, 17 November 2026. This proof retains the component line,
4: both norm signs, every fixed delta character, and the actual shorter
5: parameter endpoint. Its local maps replace the incomplete outer-line
6: step of P3K.17; it uses neither that equality nor a universal fan
7: recurrence. The earlier assertions and their correction notices remain
8: in the record.
9: 
10: ## Statement
11: 
12: Let the source and marked section be
13: \[
14:  y^2=x^3-3t^3(t-1)x+2t^4(t-1)(t-\tfrac12),\qquad
15:  G=(t^2,t^2),\qquad M=\mathcal O(G-O).
16: \]
17: Use the actual suspension over \(-3G\), with target-point
18: linearization divisor the identity component \(C_0\) of the
19: \(I_2\) fibre at \(q=1/t=0\). At the \(IV^*\) fibre use the
20: cap of order \(m=3k\), \(k>0\), and invariant vector
21: \(\ell=n(e_\gamma-e_u)+d\delta\), where \(n=\pm1\) and
22: \(d\in\mathbb Z\). Retain the original type-II line-complement
23: quotient. Denote by \(\mathcal T_-\) the negative-diagonal fan
24: of P3F.26 and by \(\mathcal T_+\) the positive-diagonal fan of
25: P3F.31. For the actual positive parameter loops the oriented
26: clutched-sphere classes are
27: \[
28: \begin{array}{c|c|c|c}
29:  \text{parameter}&\text{scalar}&\mathcal T_-&\mathcal T_+\\ \hline
30:  r&\lambda=r^{3k}&-3k&0\\
